    ],
    "text": "(3)to promote peace,goodwill, understanding andcooperation among all communities and people ofSri Lanka;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      172.87,
      279.65,
      375.46,
      290.99
    ],
    "text": "(4)to give assistance to develop worship places;",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      172.87,
      304.97,
      397.19,
      329.03
    ],
    "text": "(5)to establish information technology centers for theadvanancement of scienific studies; and",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      172.87,
      343.13,
      397.16,
      367.19
    ],
    "text": "(6)to work towards to protect and develop all rights ofwomen and children.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      381.17,
      397.19,
      455.99
    ],
    "text": "4. (1) The of the affairs of the Corporation shall, subjectto the other provisions of this Act and the rules in force forthe time being of the corporation be administered by aCommittee of Management consisting of not more thaneleven members including Chairman, Secretary, Treasurerelected in accordance with such rules.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      470.09,
      397.21,
      519.47
    ],
    "text": "(2) The first Committee of Management shall consist ofthe members of the Committee of Management of thefoundation holding office on the day immediately precedingthe date of commencement of this Act.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      157.15,
      533.57,
      397.2,
      672.23
    ],
    "text": "5.Subject to the provisions of this Act and any otherwritten law, the Corporation shall have the power to do,perform and execute all such acts, matters and thingswhatsoever as are necessary or desirable for the promotionor furtherance of all and any object of the Corporation orany one of them, including the power to open, operate andclose bank accounts, to borrow or raise moneys with orwithout security or collect or accept grants and donations,to invest its funds and to engage, employ and dismiss officersand servants required for the carrying out of the objects ofthe corporation.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
