    "text": "9. The Corporation shall be able and capable in law toacquire and hold any property, movable and immovablewhich may become vested in it by virtue of any purchase,grant, lease, gift, testamentary disposition or otherwise andall such property shall be held by the Corporation for thepurposes of this Act and subject to the rules of the Corporationmade under section 6, with power to sell, mortgage, lease,exchange or otherwise dispose of the same.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
